# XSH getuid()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XSH.getuid.001
anchor     functions/getuid.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/getuid.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      1988
says       In a child of a privileged test, after seteuid(65534) getuid()
           still returns 0, and after setuid(65534) (with privileges, all
           three user IDs) it returns 65534.
needs      root
note       The IDs are set in the setup phase with seteuid() and setuid();
           the child is UNRESOLVED when the system does not let it make
           those changes.
test       t/001-real.c

assertion  XSH.getuid.002
anchor     functions/getuid.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      2008
says       getuid() leaves errno as it was (two different values tried).
test       t/002-errno.c
